  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Pre-Play Claims**: Before play begins, check your hand for prials (three of a kind) or mournivals (four of a kind). If you have a prial, you may immediately set down two of those cards as a captured pair, keeping the third in hand. If you hold a mournival, you win all four cards immediately. 2. **Play**: Dealer's left-hand neighbor starts. On your turn: Play ONE card from your hand. Use it to capture either ONE or THREE cards of the same rank from the pool. Alternatively, play a PAIR from your hand to capture a PAIR on the table. 3. **Immediate Pair Claim**: If you hold a matching pair in hand, and another player captures a table card of that rank, you may immediately (even out of turn) add your pair to your won cards. 4. **Lying Down**: When you can no longer captureâ€”whether because you have no cards matching any on the table, or because no table cards remainâ€”you must 'Lie Down': place your entire remaining hand face-up on the table as new pool cards, and exit the round.",
    Player: "1. **Pre-Play Claims**: Before play begins, check your hand for prials (three of a kind) or mournivals (four of a kind). If you have a prial, you may immediately set down two of those cards as a captured pair, keeping the third in hand. If you hold a mournival, you win all four cards immediately. 2. **Play**: Dealer's left-hand neighbor starts. On your turn: Play ONE card from your hand. Use it to capture either ONE or THREE cards of the same rank from the pool. Alternatively, play a PAIR from your hand to capture a PAIR on the table. 3. **Immediate Pair Claim**: If you hold a matching pair in hand, and another player captures a table card of that rank, you may immediately (even out of turn) add your pair to your won cards. 4. **Lying Down**: When you can no longer captureâ€”whether because you have no cards matching any on the table, or because no table cards remainâ€”you must 'Lie Down': place your entire remaining hand face-up on the table as new pool cards, and exit the round.",
    objective: "Capture at least 4 pairs (8 cards) and avoid being the first to 'Lie Down.' Be the last player with cards in hand to win the largest share of the pot.",
    gameplay: "1. **Pre-Play Claims**: Before play begins, check your hand for prials (three of a kind) or mournivals (four of a kind). If you have a prial, you may immediately set down two of those cards as a captured pair, keeping the third in hand. If you hold a mournival, you win all four cards immediately. 2. **Play**: Dealer's left-hand neighbor starts. On your turn: Play ONE card from your hand. Use it to capture either ONE or THREE cards of the same rank from the pool. Alternatively, play a PAIR from your hand to capture a PAIR on the table. 3. **Immediate Pair Claim**: If you hold a matching pair in hand, and another player captures a table card of that rank, you may immediately (even out of turn) add your pair to your won cards. 4. **Lying Down**: When you can no longer captureâ€”whether because you have no cards matching any on the table, or because no table cards remainâ€”you must 'Lie Down': place your entire remaining hand face-up on the table as new pool cards, and exit the round.",
    keyRules: [
      'Pair = Two cards of the same rank (A-A, K-K, etc.)',
      'Prial = Three cards of the same rank (pair royal)',
      'Mournival = Four cards of the same rank',
      'If initial pool contains a mournival, dealer wins all four cards immediately.',
      'Each player puts 2 stakes into the pot; dealer puts 3 stakes.',
      'Last player with cards wins 5p from the pot.',
      'Everyone counts won cards. +/- 1p per 2 cards above or below 8 cards.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
