      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Pre-Play Claims**: Before play begins, check your hand for prials (three of a kind) or mournivals (four of a kind). If you have a prial, you may immediately set down two of those cards as a captured pair, keeping the third in hand. If you hold a mournival, you win all four cards immediately. 2. **Play**: Dealer's left-hand neighbor starts. On your turn: Play ONE card from your hand. Use it to capture either ONE or THREE cards of the same rank from the pool. Alternatively, play a PAIR from your hand to capture a PAIR on the table. 3. **Immediate Pair Claim**: If you hold a matching pair in hand, and another player captures a table card of that rank, you may immediately (even out of turn) add your pair to your won cards. 4. **Lying Down**: When you can no longer captureâ€”whether because you have no cards matching any on the table, or because no table cards remainâ€”you must 'Lie Down': place your entire remaining hand face-up on the table as new pool cards, and exit the round.",
